{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/996919-pulling-apart-the-solar-charmset-what-are-the-pieces","id":996919,"title":"Pulling apart the Solar Charmset: What are the pieces?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-01T18:27:29-07:00","id":996919,"title":"Pulling apart the Solar Charmset: What are the pieces?","content":"This seems like a weird request for assistance, but it's in pursuit of Charm design, I wanted to look Ability by Ability to see the pieces of what each &quot;piece&quot; of their Charms is, looking at obvious things like trees within the charm tree like Super Strength stuff in Athletics versus Super Speed stuff, or the more obvious divides like those in Craft or Performance. What divides do you see within each Ability, and how would you characterize them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:39:15-07:00","id":997128,"title":"","content":"Well for trees within trees, I think MadLetter did a good number on laying it out with his <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/comments/3pwiez/exalted_3e_charm_cascades/\" target=\"_blank\">visual charm trees</a>. Hope that helps a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:18:23-07:00","id":997147,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I 100% understand what you mean, but I think socialize is one of the really interesting trees to take a look at, and see what it represents. It's one of the bigger charmsets IIRC, but it has such interesting implications for what Socialize as a skill is.<br /> <br /> You've got what I like to think of as the only real social combat tree in the entire game, which can basically be summed up as the &quot;courtly intrigue&quot; tree. It starts with mastery of small manners, which basically means your Solar fits in anywhere, and branches out in two directions: The courtly intrigue offensive (starting with culture hero approach) and reactionary, which starts with unspeakable discourse technique. This branch of the charmset makes the solar an amazing harpy or spy, able to sway courts, win hearts and minds, and block her enemies.<br /> <br /> There's the defensive tree, starting with Shadow over Day, that makes your Solar's guile very high. Narratively, they seem aloof and mysterious, which fits in with the courtly-controlling puppetmaster that I feel that Socialize is well suited for. This tree continues, making your solar more and more aloof and more and more able to disguise who they truly are, that they're even able to convince themselves that they're someone else: the persona tree. It's a very intelligent, and very cool, progression of charms which makes a lot of sense to me. Also, Soul-Void kata is horrific<br /> <br /> Finally, starting with Motive-Discerning Method, there's the tree for the times you're most likely to actually roll Socialize: Read Intentions. These charms offer pretty interesting and unique benefits, letting the Solar figure out all sorts of interesting details about someone's intimacies, as well as reading deeper into them, like propensity for violence (fete-watcher stance), and what their weaknesses are (Knowing the Soul's Price).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:34:25-07:00","id":997272,"title":"","content":"Craft Functional Purpose Trees<br /> <br /> Craft Experience Tree - Brass Scales Falling +<br /> Slot Tree - Tireless Workhorse Method +<br /> Skill Augmentation Tree: Arete-Shifting Prana +<br /> Speed and Project Completion Tree - Craftsman Needs No Tool +<br /> Dice Tricks Tree - Flawless Handiwork Method +<br /> Repair and Reforging is spot on in the book as it's own section. <br /> Otherwise the efficiency, momentum, and power groups can be split several ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:05:21-07:00","id":997325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/996919-pulling-apart-the-solar-charmset-what-are-the-pieces?p=997128#post997128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well for trees within trees, I think MadLetter did a good number on laying it out with his <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/comments/3pwiez/exalted_3e_charm_cascades/\" target=\"_blank\">visual charm trees</a>. Hope that helps a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love having those cascades, but I think there' most useful for some Abilities than others.<br /> <br /> Archery, for example, has two distinct trees visually, but what the Wise Arrow tree does, and what the Phantom Arrow Technique tree does is not as direct/obvious without really getting into what each Charm does.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile visualizing Awareness shows pretty directly - despite being one tree - that there's one basic branches for each of the three Keen [Sense(s)] Technique Charms, the SAM one off, and the capstone multi-senses duo.<br /> <br /> There's also things like the Integrity Charms which because of the Bridge Keyword and a few other factors looks a lot messier in terms of thematic clusters than it probably is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T08:49:04-08:00","id":1000288,"title":"","content":"Thing about charms is that they just increase your abilities in either a skill or ability.<br /> So if you have a martial art think about what you want it to do, and then build charms around that. It is for this reason I think that some of the charms in the 3E core are in the wrong place, but that is another conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1762-rogerd","name":"RogerD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}